b/ref 17592186065438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065102 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065102 #edb/ref 1061 630730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065102 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4eb00783-0e9f-5f56-a7c2-2671083182b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065102 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065103 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065103 #edb/ref 1061 630733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065103 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a270b04-626b-5faf-b8e7-a60d62b9d521" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065103 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065113 #edb/ref 1061 630736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065113 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5f0e5f61-e451-55c5-a8ca-ae1e6b3c2676" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065113 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065139 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065139 #edb/ref 1061 1966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065139 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3d1d4c5b-f669-5ef8-ae3a-069d89747d69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065139 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065140 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065140 #edb/ref 1061 1967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065140 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0b4e1339-dcb7-5439-a531-66ef32ae8045" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065140 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065141 #edb/ref 1061 1971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065141 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91fabaf9-366a-5699-bd24-1f3331ce4790" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065141 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065178 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065178 #edb/ref 1061 27313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065178 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "55aedc57-c528-5f39-b05b-126f9ef5cee0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065178 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065333 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's find the total area of the finite region enclosed between curves the curves\n\n$$\nf(x)=x^3-2x\n$$\n\nand $g(x)=2x$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e6/e651f9df1fbc9f0f9ad8ffa49822e4e3640a3555570ca3d0f82c155c5141843e.png)\n\nFirst, we find the points where the curves intersect:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= g(x) \\\\\nx^{3} - 2x &= 2x \\\\\nx^{3} - 4x &= 0 \\\\\nx(x^{2} - 4) &= 0 \\\\\nx(x - 2)(x + 2) &= 0 \\\\\nx &= 0, 2,-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area we want consists of two symmetric regions: $A_1$ and $A_2$.\n\n![](images/4f/4fd6173127725bd771a753217002ab9656cf36a97dd37c4fe80f7d76e672ee86.png)\n\nFor the area $A_1$, we have $x \\in [-2,0]$, and the upper function is $f(x)$ while the lower function is $g(x)$. So, the area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{1} &= \\int_{-2}^{0}(f(x) - g(x))dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}((x^{3} - 2x) - 2x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}(x^{3} - 4x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}x^{3}dx - 4\\int_{-2}^{0}xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right|_{-2}^{0} - 4 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right|_{-2}^{0} \\\\\n&= (0 - 4) - 4(0 - 2) \\\\\n&=-4 + 8 \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the regions are symmetric, we have that $A_2=A_1=4$.\n\nFinally, the required area is given by\n\n$$\nA = A_1 + A_2 = 4 + 4 = 8\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065333 #edb/ref 1065 1003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065333 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "988c723b-81d1-541c-9ab3-bebbece1cf06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065333 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065432 #edb/ref 1064 "At first sight, the integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int x \\sqrt{x+2} \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nmight not seem like it can be solved using substitution because $x$ is not the derivative of $x+2.$ But in fact, with some clever manipulation, we can indeed solve it using substitution!\n\nSetting\n\n$$\nu=x+2,\n$$\n\nand computing the required derivatives gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int x \\sqrt{x+2} \\,\\textrm{d}x=\\int x \\sqrt{u} \\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nSo we still have an $x$ in our integrand. However, we can get rid of it by solving for $x$ in the rule $u=x+2.$ We get\n\n$$\nx=u-2,\n$$\n\nand using this, the integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u= & \\int (u-2)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int (u-2){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral by multiplying out the product and integrating the resulting function with respect to $u\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (u-2){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\int ({u}^{3/2}-2{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u-2\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{4}{3}{u}^{3/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the final step, we substitute $u=x+2,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{5}(x+2)^{5/2}-\\frac{4}{3}(x+2)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x+2)^{5}}-\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x+2)^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065432 #edb/ref 1065 843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065432 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6d16cf43-c7f8-5600-82a2-55a301cc5a4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065432 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065438 #edb/ref 1064 "How do we calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\dfrac{3x+2}{x+2}\\,\\textrm d x\\,?$\n\nWe need to write the integrand so that it's something we can integrate. One way to do this is to divide $3x+2$ by $x+2$ using polynomial or synthetic division. We'll use synthetic division because it's faster. \n\nTo rewrite $\\dfrac{3x+2}{x+2},$ we complete a synthetic division table.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}-2$ | $3$ | $2$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ |\n\nThis tells us that $\\dfrac{3x+2}{x+2}$ can be decomposed into a quotient and remainder as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x+2}{x+2}= 3 - \\dfrac{4}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can integrate the function, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3-\\frac{4}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065438 #edb/ref 1065 884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065438 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2437a8a0-d1de-5b85-8577-7e7493c4d520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065438 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1039 "Integrating a Logarithmic Expression Using Cyclic Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "df0c3b59-7667-53e9-84d3-bba30ea116fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186